---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { AUTHOR_EMAIL, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';

// About and Contact are one page, in that order. A one-person masthead and a
// way to reach that person are the same disclosure — splitting them across two
// routes made each half look thinner than it was.
//
// The old /contact channel block (editorial / tips / general, all pointing at
// the same mailbox) is gone: three buttons resolving to one address is
// theatre. One address, stated once.
//
// The mission runs as two columns rather than a 672px measure. It is the
// longest continuous stretch of prose on the site and the only page where the
// reader is deciding whether to trust the publication at all; a single narrow
// column made it look like a wall to get through.
const mailto = `mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`;
---
<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Who's behind Vantage, what it stands for, and how to reach them."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-6 sm:px-10 py-11 sm:py-14">
    <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-[0.09em] mb-4">About</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-[56px] font-display font-bold text-content leading-[1.02] tracking-[-0.025em] mb-5 max-w-[900px]">
      What you understand depends on where you stand.
    </h1>
    <div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-teal mb-9"></div>

    <div class="grid gap-9 md:grid-cols-2 mb-14">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-[17px] leading-[1.72] text-content/78 text-justify">
        <p>
          Vantage is a Philippine news and media company built on the idea contained in
          its name. We cover the issues the country is arguing about right now, and our
          work is to make those arguments legible: what is actually being proposed, who
          stands to gain or lose, and what has already been tried. We follow decisions
          from the offices where they are drafted to the communities where they land, in
          Metro Manila and well outside it. Being useful to our readers matters more to
          us than being first to publish.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are working toward a Philippines where public life is conducted in front of
          an informed audience, where the people affected by a decision understand it well
          enough to question it. That means building a newsroom Filipinos return to out of
          habit rather than accident, and producing journalism that still holds up a year
          after it runs.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-[17px] leading-[1.72] text-content/78 text-justify">
        <p>
          It also means treating our readers as participants rather than traffic: people
          with their own vantage points, whose questions shape what we pursue next.
        </p>
        <p>
          Accuracy is our first obligation, and we would rather be late than wrong. We
          report independently, without deference to advertisers, political patrons, or
          the pressure of a trending topic. We stay close to the ground, because distance
          is how stories get flattened into abstractions. We show our work: naming sources
          where we safely can, explaining how we know what we know, and correcting errors
          openly and quickly rather than quietly. And we write plainly, on the conviction
          that anything worth reporting can be explained clearly to anyone willing to read
          it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-[0.09em] mb-4">Masthead</p>
    <div class="bg-surface border border-content/10 rounded-2xl p-7 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr] items-center mb-14 v-rise">
      <img
        src="/masthead/jairus-macabuhay.jpg"
        alt="Sir Jairus Macabuhay"
        width="200"
        height="200"
        loading="lazy"
        class="w-[200px] h-[200px] rounded-xl object-cover bg-ground"
      />
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[30px] font-display font-bold text-content leading-tight mb-1.5">Sir Jairus Macabuhay</h2>
        <p class="text-[15px] font-medium text-accent mb-2">Founder & Editor-in-Chief</p>
        <a href={`mailto:${AUTHOR_EMAIL}`} class="masthead-mail inline-block text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline pb-1 mb-4">{AUTHOR_EMAIL}</a>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-content/72 max-w-[620px]">
          Vantage is a one-person newsroom. Every explainer on this site was reported,
          written, checked and published by the same person, and the byline says so on
          purpose.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 mb-14">
      <div class="bg-surface border border-content/10 rounded-2xl p-7 v-rise">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-[0.09em] mb-3">Independence</p>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold text-content leading-tight mb-3.5">
          Self-funded, and we will say if that changes.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-[1.68] text-content/72">
          We receive no money from political parties, campaigns, government agencies,
          corporations, or advocacy groups, and no outside organization has any say in
          what we cover or how we cover it. If that ever changes, we will say so here,
          plainly and before you have to ask.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-surface border border-content/10 rounded-2xl p-7 v-rise">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-[0.09em] mb-3">Corrections</p>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold text-content leading-tight mb-3.5">
          We fix it, and we say what we fixed.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-[1.68] text-content/72 mb-4">
          Corrections are noted on the story itself, with the date and the nature of the
          error. Nothing gets quietly edited after publication.
        </p>
        {/* A running count, stated plainly. "None so far" is a claim a
            publication should be willing to print and then have to update. */}
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 px-3.5 py-3 bg-ground rounded-[10px]">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-teal shrink-0"></span>
          <span class="text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-content/70">No corrections issued to date.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* The one highlight moment on the page, and the only place the address
        appears. Deliberately unlabelled by purpose: tips, questions and
        corrections all land in the same inbox, so naming one of them would
        imply the others belong somewhere else. Fixed brand colours, not the
        semantic tokens — this block brings its own ground in both modes. */}
    <div class="bg-teal-light rounded-2xl p-8 sm:p-10 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-end justify-between gap-8 v-rise">
      <div>
        <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-teal-dark uppercase tracking-[0.09em] mb-3.5">Contact</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-[40px] font-display font-bold text-teal-dark leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.02em] mb-3.5">
          Tips, questions, corrections.
        </h2>
        <p class="max-w-[520px] text-base leading-relaxed text-teal-dark/78">
          One inbox, read by the person who writes the stories. Naming three addresses
          that all resolve to the same mailbox would be theatre.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a
        href={mailto}
        class="shrink-0 bg-teal-dark text-teal-light rounded-xl px-6 py-4 text-base font-medium no-underline transition-[transform,background-color] duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:bg-ink"
      >{CONTACT_EMAIL} →</a>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* The rule retracts on hover rather than drawing in — it is already the
     resting state here, because the address is the point of the block. */
  .masthead-mail {
    background-image: linear-gradient(var(--color-teal), var(--color-teal));
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    background-position: 0 100%;
    background-size: 100% 2px;
    transition: background-size 0.25s ease;
  }
  .masthead-mail:hover {
    background-size: 0% 2px;
  }
</style>
